From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:21:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 012/105] fix(adaptive): make --speculative-adaptive sound for
 qwen4_exp (GDN recovery fence, per-state QSA index share, per-state recovery
 graphs)

- activate runtime states only at activate_step_by_batch; on_verify_complete just records
- drain the outgoing HybridLinearAttnBackend recovery stream before swapping backends
- capture GDN recovery CUDA graphs for every adaptive state's target backend
- one QSAMTPSharedSparseIndices per state (tail_width = steps + 1) instead of disabling
  index sharing under adaptive
- override cuda_graph_config.decode (what capture actually reads) and skip unreachable states
- decode graph runner warmup hook uses the runner's own backend
- adaptive_two_state.json: candidate steps [3, 15] with wide hysteresis

Implemented by Codex (gpt-5.6-sol high) from a supervisor spec; CPU tests added.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
